{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-439567-r4523381","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Snickerdoodles (Idaho Daily Statesman)","sourcePageId":439567,"sourceRevision":"4523381","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-07-13T18:01:21Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Snickerdoodles%20(Idaho%20Daily%20Statesman)&oldid=4523381","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:17:33.011Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Dessert recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for snickerdoodles","Category:Recipes using baking soda","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using cow milk","Category:Recipes using cream of tartar","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Recipes using white sugar","Category:Recipes without cooking time"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"0ca99a93baa842059dde476b56461f57a8e6d6b55bebf8770b40f335fc27eb07","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe}}\n\n{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Cookie recipes\n| Servings = 24\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\nThis recipe is from the Idaho Daily Statesman (Boise, Idaho), October 20, 1901, pg. 11. Per the source:<blockquote>''\"Snickerdoodles\" is the somewhat fantastic name of quickly made little cakes especially dear to the children's heart. A recipe for them copied from an old scrapbook [follows].''</blockquote>\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] white granulated [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]]\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:Milk|milk]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Baking Soda|baking soda]]\n* 2½ cups [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n* 2 tsp [[Cookbook:Cream of Tartar|cream of tartar]]\n* ½ tsp [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|Cinnamon]]\n* Sugar\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n# Stir together sugar and butter until creamy.\n# Add eggs.\n# Dissolve baking soda in milk, then add.\n# Add flour, cream of tartar and salt.\n# [[Cookbook:Beating|Beat]] the batter thoroughly.\n# Pour in shallow pans.\n# Dust the top of the cake with cinnamon and sugar.\n# [[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] for 15 minutes.\n# Cool, then cut in squares.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for snickerdoodles]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Dessert recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking soda]]\n[[Category:Recipes using white sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cream of tartar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cow milk]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Snickerdoodles (Idaho Daily Statesman)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"24","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 cups white granulated sugar","sourceText":"2 cups white granulated sugar","amountText":"2 cups white granulated sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"½ cup butter","sourceText":"½ cup butter","amountText":"½ cup butter","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"2 eggs","sourceText":"2 eggs","amountText":"2 eggs","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 cup milk","sourceText":"1 c